      "id": "RB-307",
      "title": "High error rate with saturated resources",
      "content": "Possible causes: traffic surge, a retry storm, a regression that increases CPU per request, too few instances. Compare request rate with the baseline and look at autoscaling."
    },
    {
      "id": "RB-007",
      "title": "General HTTP 5xx investigation checklist",
      "content": "1. Find the first error in the logs and note the time. 2. Check recent deploys of the affected service near that time. 3. Check dependencies (database, payment gateway, cache). 4. Compare error rate before and after the change."
    },
